1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,830
Imagine this.

2
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,590
You buy a brand-new BYD.

3
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:03,390
A few months later,

4
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:07,430
you hit a kangaroo on the motorway
at 110 kilometres an hour.

5
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:09,190
Your insurance accepts the claim.

6
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:10,370
The parts are ordered.

7
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:11,890
And then… nothing.

8
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:15,090
Eleven weeks later, your car is
still sitting at the smash repairer.

9
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:19,010
And the supplier tells you the missing
parts are another eight weeks away.

10
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,430
That's not a made-up story.

11
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:24,790
It's what one BYD owner described
publicly on an Aussie car forum in early

12
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,310
2025 and it wasn't the only one.

13
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:30,170
Parts delays, calls that go unanswered,

14
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:33,310
and long waits just to get a car looked
at became some of the most common

15
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:35,650
complaints in BYD owner groups.

16
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:38,670
Today, BYD is one of the
biggest car brands in Australia.

17
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:40,630
So what went wrong after the sale?

18
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:44,150
How expensive is a BYD to
repair and insure, really?

19
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,250
And has BYD actually fixed it?

20
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:50,290
Because in October 2026, BYD
made a very big announcement.

21
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:51,530
Stay with me to the end,

22
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:54,820
because what it means for you
depends on which BYD you drive.

23
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:57,696
First, let's understand
how fast this happened.

24
00:00:57,746 --> 00:01:02,536
BYD arrived in Australia with one
model, the Atto 3 electric SUV.

25
00:01:02,586 --> 00:01:04,376
Within a few years, it had a full range:

26
00:01:04,426 --> 00:01:08,216
the Dolphin, the Seal, the
Sealion 6 and Sealion 7,

27
00:01:08,266 --> 00:01:15,076
the Shark 6 ute, and now even a budget
EV, the Atto 1, priced from $19,990.

28
00:01:15,126 --> 00:01:20,556
In the first half of 2026, BYD sold
more than 52,000 cars in Australia.

29
00:01:20,606 --> 00:01:23,196
In March, it broke into the top
three brands in the country.

30
00:01:23,246 --> 00:01:28,096
By October, BYD said it had more
than 150,000 customers here.

31
00:01:28,146 --> 00:01:29,476
That's incredible growth.

32
00:01:29,526 --> 00:01:33,006
But it created a problem that every
fast-growing brand eventually hits.

33
00:01:33,056 --> 00:01:34,936
Selling cars is one thing.

34
00:01:34,986 --> 00:01:36,536
Fixing them is another.

35
00:01:36,586 --> 00:01:39,886
Every one of those 150,000
cars will need servicing,

36
00:01:39,936 --> 00:01:43,936
tyres, windscreens, and
sooner or later crash repairs.

37
00:01:43,986 --> 00:01:47,306
And the network to support them
didn't grow as fast as the sales did.

38
00:01:48,023 --> 00:01:49,303
Let's start with parts.

39
00:01:49,353 --> 00:01:53,913
Australia is a small market compared
to China, Europe or the United States.

40
00:01:53,963 --> 00:01:55,573
When a part isn't stocked locally,

41
00:01:55,623 --> 00:01:58,353
it has to be shipped, and
that can take weeks or months.

42
00:01:58,403 --> 00:02:01,293
BYD's own executives have
been open about this.

43
00:02:01,343 --> 00:02:05,153
When Stephen Collins took over as BYD
Australia's chief operating officer,

44
00:02:05,203 --> 00:02:08,813
he spoke publicly about how the brand
needed to shake off its reputation for

45
00:02:08,863 --> 00:02:11,093
long service and parts delays.

46
00:02:11,143 --> 00:02:14,853
CarsGuide reported that months-long
parts delays and unanswered emails and

47
00:02:14,903 --> 00:02:17,953
calls were among the most common
complaints in owner groups,

48
00:02:18,003 --> 00:02:20,693
with some posts attracting
thousands of responses.

49
00:02:20,743 --> 00:02:22,173
And there was another issue.

50
00:02:22,223 --> 00:02:25,593
Mark Harland, the boss of
BYD's premium brand Denza,

51
00:02:25,643 --> 00:02:27,253
admitted that in the early days,

52
00:02:27,303 --> 00:02:30,793
even basic things like repair training
and the right tools weren't in place

53
00:02:30,843 --> 00:02:31,773
everywhere.

54
00:02:31,823 --> 00:02:33,453
Even if a workshop had the part,

55
00:02:33,503 --> 00:02:35,773
did they have the training
to fit it on an EV?

56
00:02:35,823 --> 00:02:36,623
Not always.

57
00:02:37,395 --> 00:02:40,405
Now, to be fair, this
isn't only a BYD problem.

58
00:02:40,455 --> 00:02:41,395
In July 2026,

59
00:02:41,445 --> 00:02:45,885
the Australian Automotive Dealer Association
released an independent review by

60
00:02:45,935 --> 00:02:48,005
Emeritus Professor Jenny Buchan.

61
00:02:48,055 --> 00:02:51,545
The review found that customers across
the industry face long delays to get

62
00:02:51,595 --> 00:02:54,785
their cars fixed especially
electric vehicles.

63
00:02:54,835 --> 00:02:57,965
Dealers told the review that workshop
backlogs could stretch to six to eight

64
00:02:58,015 --> 00:03:00,005
weeks just to diagnose a problem.

65
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:00,845
Not fix it.

66
00:03:00,895 --> 00:03:02,385
Just find out what's wrong.

67
00:03:02,435 --> 00:03:04,425
Combine that with slow parts and, often,

68
00:03:04,475 --> 00:03:08,665
no loan car, and owners can be left
without transport for a very long time.

69
00:03:08,715 --> 00:03:12,065
The report also pointed
at the wave of new brands.

70
00:03:12,115 --> 00:03:15,585
Australia has more than seventy car
brands competing for around 1.2 million

71
00:03:15,635 --> 00:03:16,985
sales a year.

72
00:03:17,035 --> 00:03:21,225
Denza, Geely, IM Motors and
GAC have all arrived recently.

73
00:03:21,275 --> 00:03:23,405
Not all of them have the parts warehouses,

74
00:03:23,455 --> 00:03:26,845
trained technicians and dealer networks
that the long-established brands built

75
00:03:26,895 --> 00:03:27,775
over decades.

76
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:30,100
So what about cost?

77
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:33,860
You'll see lots of scary numbers
online about BYD repair bills.

78
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:36,380
Here's what we can actually back up.

79
00:03:36,430 --> 00:03:40,820
EVs and plug-in hybrids are generally
more expensive to repair after a crash.

80
00:03:40,870 --> 00:03:44,900
A senior figure in BYD's collision
repair network told the industry magazine

81
00:03:44,950 --> 00:03:49,000
Paint and Panel that EV repair costs
currently sit in a category more like

82
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:50,160
high-end luxury cars.

83
00:03:50,210 --> 00:03:52,640
That pushes insurance premiums up.

84
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:55,320
The battery is the big
one if it's badly damaged,

85
00:03:55,370 --> 00:03:56,400
a car can be written off,

86
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:59,720
because the battery is such a
large share of the car's value.

87
00:03:59,770 --> 00:04:01,420
It's not just the battery, either.

88
00:04:01,470 --> 00:04:02,740
Take the Shark 6.

89
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:04,880
A rear bumper isn't just plastic anymore.

90
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:07,860
It carries the reversing
camera and parking sensors.

91
00:04:07,910 --> 00:04:11,460
A low-speed car park bump that used
to cost a few hundred dollars can turn

92
00:04:11,510 --> 00:04:13,940
into new sensors plus recalibration.

93
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:16,260
But here's the part a
lot of videos leave out.

94
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:20,230
Insurance comparison site Compare the
Market quoted twenty popular hybrids,

95
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:22,680
plug-ins and EVs across eleven insurers.

96
00:04:22,730 --> 00:04:28,760
The BYD Dolphin averaged about
$1,425 a year less than a Toyota

97
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:29,900
Corolla hybrid.

98
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:33,000
The Sealion 7 came in
just under a RAV4 hybrid.

99
00:04:33,050 --> 00:04:36,960
The Shark 6 was higher,
at around $2,071 a year,

100
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:40,780
but still well below the two
Teslas, which were over $3,000.

101
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:41,980
So the honest answer is:

102
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:46,980
BYD repairs can cost more than an old
petrol car, especially for crash damage.

103
00:04:47,030 --> 00:04:51,000
But BYD insurance isn't automatically
more expensive than its Japanese rivals.

104
00:04:51,050 --> 00:04:53,110
It depends heavily on the model.

105
00:04:53,926 --> 00:04:56,636
Before we get to BYD's fix, quick favour.

106
00:04:56,686 --> 00:05:00,136
If you own a BYD or you're thinking
about buying one tell me in the comments

107
00:05:00,186 --> 00:05:02,696
what your service and
repair experience has been.

108
00:05:02,746 --> 00:05:03,636
Good or bad.

109
00:05:03,686 --> 00:05:05,936
Your experience helps
other Aussies decide.

110
00:05:05,986 --> 00:05:10,176
And if you want honest, fact-checked
car videos for Australia, hit subscribe.

111
00:05:10,226 --> 00:05:12,766
It costs nothing and it
keeps this channel going.

112
00:05:13,525 --> 00:05:15,175
There's one more thing worth mentioning.

113
00:05:15,225 --> 00:05:21,255
In 2026, BYD recalled 32,009 Shark 6
utes in Australia because of possible

114
00:05:21,305 --> 00:05:23,795
abnormal wear in the spare wheel assembly.

115
00:05:23,845 --> 00:05:27,615
BYD advised affected owners to remove
the spare wheel if they wanted to keep

116
00:05:27,665 --> 00:05:29,335
driving before the fix.

117
00:05:29,385 --> 00:05:33,055
Recalls happen to every brand
Toyota, Ford, all of them.

118
00:05:33,105 --> 00:05:35,275
A recall is actually the system working.

119
00:05:35,325 --> 00:05:39,175
But for a brand already fighting a
reputation for slow after-sales support,

120
00:05:39,225 --> 00:05:42,535
a recall of more than thirty thousand
utes adds pressure on dealers and

121
00:05:42,585 --> 00:05:44,325
workshops that were already busy.

122
00:05:45,117 --> 00:05:47,407
So, has BYD done anything about it?

123
00:05:47,457 --> 00:05:49,847
Yes and it's big.

124
00:05:49,897 --> 00:05:52,207
On the 20th of October 2026,

125
00:05:52,257 --> 00:05:57,087
BYD Australia announced that it now
holds more than 580,000 parts for BYD and

126
00:05:57,137 --> 00:05:59,227
Denza models on Australian soil.

127
00:05:59,277 --> 00:06:03,487
That's around 95 per cent of the parts
for both ranges, kept in stock locally.

128
00:06:03,537 --> 00:06:07,407
The value of those parts is more
than $25 million at any time,

129
00:06:07,457 --> 00:06:11,347
spread across more than 24,000 square
metres of warehouses in four cities.

130
00:06:11,397 --> 00:06:13,307
The biggest is in Melbourne,

131
00:06:13,357 --> 00:06:16,837
with about 15,000 square metres
and a team of around forty people.

132
00:06:16,887 --> 00:06:20,617
BYD says dealers close to a warehouse
should get in-stock parts within

133
00:06:20,667 --> 00:06:24,507
twenty-four hours, and remote or
rural areas within about a week.

134
00:06:24,557 --> 00:06:28,787
Importantly, BYD says it now keeps
Blade battery packs in local stock and

135
00:06:28,837 --> 00:06:32,447
batteries are one of the slowest parts
to get when they have to come by ship.

136
00:06:32,497 --> 00:06:36,007
Chief operating officer Stephen Collins
summed up the message like this:

137
00:06:36,057 --> 00:06:39,327
"Our commitment to Australian
customers doesn't end at the handover.

138
00:06:39,377 --> 00:06:43,587
It starts there." BYD also set up its
own approved collision repair network

139
00:06:43,637 --> 00:06:46,947
early, and many of those shops
were already trained on Teslas,

140
00:06:46,997 --> 00:06:49,467
so they had the EV
equipment and experience.

141
00:06:49,517 --> 00:06:50,757
That's a smart shortcut.

142
00:06:51,491 --> 00:06:53,801
Now, if you're stuck waiting
on a repair right now,

143
00:06:53,851 --> 00:06:55,801
here's something every Aussie should know.

144
00:06:55,851 --> 00:06:57,701
Under the Australian Consumer Law,

145
00:06:57,751 --> 00:07:01,241
manufacturers and importers must make
spare parts and repair facilities

146
00:07:01,291 --> 00:07:04,621
available for a reasonable
time after you buy a product.

147
00:07:04,671 --> 00:07:07,921
That applies even if you didn't
buy it directly from them.

148
00:07:07,971 --> 00:07:10,921
The problem, as the dealer
association's review pointed out,

149
00:07:10,971 --> 00:07:13,001
is that "reasonable" is vague.

150
00:07:13,051 --> 00:07:14,941
The review called for clearer rules,

151
00:07:14,991 --> 00:07:17,821
including on battery
degradation and replacement.

152
00:07:17,871 --> 00:07:18,841
Until that happens,

153
00:07:18,891 --> 00:07:21,741
the best thing you can do is
keep everything in writing,

154
00:07:21,791 --> 00:07:25,601
contact the manufacturer's head office
directly not just the dealer and if it

155
00:07:25,651 --> 00:07:28,501
drags on, go to your
state's fair trading office.

156
00:07:28,551 --> 00:07:32,241
There's also the Motor Vehicle Service
and Repair Information Sharing Scheme,

157
00:07:32,291 --> 00:07:34,161
which came in from 2022.

158
00:07:34,211 --> 00:07:38,341
It requires car makers to share repair
information with independent workshops.

159
00:07:38,391 --> 00:07:42,261
But the Insurance Council has raised
concerns that some brands still restrict

160
00:07:42,311 --> 00:07:43,881
parts sales to their own dealers,

161
00:07:43,931 --> 00:07:46,951
which limits how many workshops
can actually do the job.

162
00:07:47,694 --> 00:07:50,204
So, is BYD's repair problem real?

163
00:07:50,254 --> 00:07:50,694
Yes.

164
00:07:50,744 --> 00:07:53,744
Owners waited far too long
for parts in the early years,

165
00:07:53,794 --> 00:07:55,844
and the brand itself has admitted it.

166
00:07:55,894 --> 00:07:58,364
Are BYD cars more expensive to repair?

167
00:07:58,414 --> 00:08:00,537
For crash damage on EVs and plug-ins,

168
00:08:00,587 --> 00:08:05,024
usually yes but insurance on models
like the Dolphin and Sealion 7 is

169
00:08:05,074 --> 00:08:08,644
competitive, and sometimes cheaper
than the Toyota equivalent.

170
00:08:08,694 --> 00:08:10,144
And has it been fixed?

171
00:08:10,194 --> 00:08:14,784
BYD has put real money into the
problem $25 million of parts and four

172
00:08:14,834 --> 00:08:18,084
warehouses is not a press
release with nothing behind it.

173
00:08:18,134 --> 00:08:21,304
The real test is whether owners notice
the difference over the next twelve

174
00:08:21,354 --> 00:08:21,764
months.

175
00:08:21,814 --> 00:08:25,264
Because a warehouse full of parts
only helps if the workshops,

176
00:08:25,314 --> 00:08:28,064
the technicians and the
phone lines keep up too.

177
00:08:28,114 --> 00:08:31,524
If you're buying a BYD today,
ask the dealer three questions.

178
00:08:31,574 --> 00:08:33,784
Where is the nearest
approved collision repairer?

179
00:08:33,834 --> 00:08:35,924
How long are current service bookings?

180
00:08:35,974 --> 00:08:38,524
And what's the loan car policy
if the car is off the road?

181
00:08:38,574 --> 00:08:41,274
The answers will tell you
more than any brochure.

182
00:08:42,010 --> 00:08:45,660
That's the full, honest story of
BYD's repair problem in Australia.

183
00:08:45,710 --> 00:08:46,620
If this helped you,

184
00:08:46,670 --> 00:08:50,480
hit that like button and subscribe we've
got new videos every week on what's

185
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:52,680
really going on in the Aussie car market.

186
00:08:52,730 --> 00:08:56,880
Drop a comment and tell me:
would you buy a BYD in 2026?

187
00:08:56,930 --> 00:08:59,620
And if you want to see which other
brands are struggling right now,

188
00:08:59,670 --> 00:09:03,400
the next video is ten car brands
in serious trouble in Australia.

189
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:05,060
Some of them might surprise you.

190
00:09:05,110 --> 00:09:05,910
See you there.
